{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters","id":1356915,"title":"How Would You Stat Game Characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-25T04:26:02-08:00","id":1356915,"title":"How Would You Stat Game Characters?","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">As in, Witcher, Castlevania, even Far Cry Primal?</span></span></span><ul><li>What would their caste be?</li> <li>Their supernal?</li> <li>Their caste/favored?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T04:44:32-08:00","id":1356916,"title":"","content":"Depends on what I'm using them for. I've argued, for instance, that Batman could be represented fairly solidly as any Caste of Solar; Simon Belmont seems like a good Zenith or Dawn, but the deciding factor would probably be what role he's going to serve in my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T08:41:50-08:00","id":1356927,"title":"","content":"The Witcher is an odd one, because Geralt is actually a mutant created by magic, and so one could argue that he's a mortal turned into a Witcher by a sorcerous working.<br /> The other thing of course is, while overall he tends to be rather Dawn-ish (Melee-supernal, Dodge, Thrown, Resistance), although with good ratings in Twilight abilities, he does have various spells that really don't fit Exalted's style, it's more DnD.<br /> I guess you could have him as a Dawn with Hypnotic Tongue Technique, and a ranged magical attack (Aard for Withering, Igni for Decisive), but I'm not sure how you would do Quen or Yrden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-25-2019, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T09:54:55-08:00","id":1356932,"title":"","content":"Geralt<br /> Witcher<br /> <br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <br /> Charisma 3<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Appearance 3<br /> <br /> Perception 4<br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Melee 4 (Swords)<br /> Brawl 2<br /> Occult 3 (Monsters, Witchers)<br /> Lore 2 <br /> Craft: Alchemy 3<br /> Craft: Weapons 4 (Silver Swords)<br /> Craft: Armor 4 (Wolf School Medium Armor)<br /> Craft: Artifacts 3<br /> Dodge 3 (Monsters)<br /> Athletics 3<br /> Medicine 2 (Potions)<br /> Thrown 2<br /> Resistance 4<br /> Integrity 4<br /> Presence 2 (Intimidation)<br /> Socailize 3 (Outcast)<br /> Awareness 3 (Ambushes)<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Stealth 2<br /> Ride 2<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Survival 3<br /> <br /> Willpower 7<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Exalted Healing<br /> Igni Sign (as The Burning Name)<br /> Aard Sign (as Igni but with Smashing instead of setting things on fire)<br /> Quen Sign (1 WP: gain Hardness 10/scene)<br /> Yrden (1 WP: supplemented social influence roll against a single target takes no penalty for unbelievable claims and doesn't need a supporting intimacy)<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Initiation: Witcher<br /> <br /> Defining Tie: Ciri (father's love)<br /> Major Tie: Yennifer (Masochistic love)<br /> Minor Tie: Dandilion (brotherly love)<br /> Minor Tie: Wolf School Witchers (brotherhood)<br /> Minor Tie: Triss (love)<br /> Defining Principle: I protect people from monsters<br /> Minor Principle: Witcher's Code<br /> Minor Principle: I like playing Gwent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-26-2019, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T01:54:00-08:00","id":1357005,"title":"","content":"Reinhardt Schneider<br /> Heroic Mortal<br /> Vampire Hunter<br /> <br /> Strength 4<br /> Dexterity 2<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <br /> Charisma 2<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Appearance 3<br /> <br /> Perception 2<br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Archery 1<br /> Brawl 1<br /> Melee 4 (Whip)<br /> Thrown 2<br /> War 1<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Lore 2<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 3 (Vampires)<br /> <br /> Athletics 3<br /> Awareness 2<br /> Dodge 2 <br /> <br /> Integrity 4<br /> Resistance 3<br /> Socailize 2<br /> <br /> Presence 2<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Allies 3 (Carrie)<br /> Artifact 4 (Vampire Killer, Attuned for 1 WP)<br /> Resources 2 (Fallen nobility)<br /> Belmont Bloodline<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> <br /> Defining Principle: I will defeat Dracula and end the Night<br /> Major Principle: I am the shield that protects the innocent<br /> Minor Pinciple: Christianity<br /> Defining Tie: Dracula (Cold hatred)<br /> Major Tie: Carrie Fernandez (Respected partner)<br /> Major Tie: Rosa (love)<br /> Minor Tie: Michael Gelhart Schneider (Father)<br /> Minor Tie: Henry Oldrey (Respected partner)<br /> <br /> <br /> Artifact 4 - Vampire Killer - Alchemical Whip<br /> <br /> The whip that will destroy all who are related to the kindred of the night.<br /> <br /> Crafted by Baron Leon Belmont and used by his descendants, this holy alchemical whip is empowered to fight vampires, demons and the forces of darkness. It is the Vampire Killer.<br /> <br /> Attunement: Not made of Creation's magical materials, only those descendend from Leon Belmont can be Resonant with this Artifact. All other users are Dissonant, save Solars who are neutral by virtue of their mastery of all artifacts. A mortal who takes up an oath to thwart Dracula may attune to Vampire Killer for 1WP, but uses it as if Dissonant unless they are a Belmont, in which case they become Resonant. Creatures of Darkness are always Dissonant, even if they are a Belmont.<br /> <br /> Leon's Oath - Permanent<br /> A character who attunes to Vampire Killer gains a Defining Principle of &quot;I will stop Dracula and end the Night&quot;, which cannot be weakened.<br /> <br /> This Evocation awakens at no cost when attuning to Vampire Killer<br /> <br /> Night's Bane - Permanent - Dissonant/Resonant<br /> Vampire Killer deals Aggravated damage to Creatures of Darkness, and provides a +2 Clash bonus (which does not stack with wielding two weapons).<br /> Resonant: This Evocation awakens for free when attuning to Vampire Killer<br /> Dissonant: This Evocation cannot be awakened.<br /> <br /> Sara's Sacrifice - Permanent - Resonant/Dissonant<br /> Vampire Killer's Decisive attacks ignore the Hardness of Creatures of Darkness. The whip may strike incorporeal foes, and may harm beings who otherwise by rights should not be harmed by the strike of a whip, so long as they are Creatures of Darkness.<br /> Dissonant: The wielder may pay 1WP to allow Vampire Killer to ignore the Hardness of Creatures of Darkness for one Scene (but this Evocation provides no other benefit)<br /> Resonant: This Evocation awakens for free when first confronting a powerful force of darkness. Additionally the wielder of Vampire Killer may automatically sense if a being is a Creature of Darkness unless they are magically concealing their nature, in which case this Evocation allows the wielder to contest even otherwise perfect magical obfuscation of a Creature of Darkness's nature with an appropriate contested roll (such as Perception+Awareness, or Wits+Occult, vs whatever magic being used), but provides no other bonuses to such a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-26-2019, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T02:55:31-08:00","id":1357012,"title":"","content":"The Hero of Time<br /> Exigent of Courage<br /> <br /> Strength 2 (6)<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 3<br /> <br /> Charisma 3<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 3<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Archery 3<br /> Brawl <br /> Melee 4 (Sword)<br /> Thrown 2 (Bombs)<br /> War 1 (Soliders of Hyrule)<br /> <br /> Craft<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Lore 2<br /> Medicine <br /> Occult 1<br /> <br /> Athletics 3<br /> Awareness 2 (Hey Listen)<br /> Dodge 3<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Stealth 1<br /> <br /> Integrity 3 <br /> Resistance 2<br /> Ride 3 (Epona)<br /> Sail 3<br /> Survival 3<br /> <br /> Beurocracy <br /> Investigation<br /> Performance 4<br /> Presence 2<br /> Socailize 2<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Allies 3 (Navi)<br /> Artifact 4 (Master Sword)<br /> Artifact 4 (Bow of Light)<br /> Artifact 3 (Goron Strength)<br /> Mentor 3 (Princess Zelda, Exigent of Wisdom)<br /> Familiar 3 (Epona, the horse which is always a whistle away)<br /> Resources 4 (large rupee wallet)<br /> <br /> Willpower 8<br /> Essence 3 (19/47, 15 committed)<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Heart Containers - The Hero of Time has -0\u00d78, -1\u00d78, -2\u00d78, -4\u00d75, Incapx5.<br /> Courage Prevails - The Hero of Time has dice caps as a Solar, but may spend 6m to add three successes to any roll, or raise a static value by 3.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> You could do Link as a Solar and Zelda as a Lunar... I might do so later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-26-2019, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T19:24:18-08:00","id":1357150,"title":"","content":"&quot;You could do Link as a Solar and Zelda as a Lunar... I might do so later&quot;<br /> <br /> One of these has turned into a wolf and a rabbit and it ain't zelda<br /> <br /> And a Fishman, plantboy, and rockeater","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T23:54:10-08:00","id":1357172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357150#post1357150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;You could do Link as a Solar and Zelda as a Lunar... I might do so later&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> One of these has turned into a wolf and a rabbit and it ain't zelda<br /> <br /> And a Fishman, plantboy, and rockeater</div> </div> </div> </div>Link is transformed into those things by an outside source. He doesn't transform on his own power.<br /> <br /> Unlike Zelda to Shiek.<br /> <br /> Plus Link's powers ring more Solar to me -- Blazing Solar Bolt and the like.<br /> <br /> Plus Link's theme of being a reborn hero, returning to save the world from strife is closer to Solar than the Lunar themes of being Stewards to a world in crisis.<br /> <br /> Plus the way Lunar Bond works now is much closer for Zelda getting a power-up around Link.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you want to do Link as a Lunar please do! I'd love to see it. It's a cool idea. FMA never posts in their own threads here (they're all reddit cross <br /> -posts), so if this interests you go nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T12:28:25-08:00","id":1357233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357172#post1357172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Link is transformed into those things by an outside source. He doesn't transform on his own power.<br /> <br /> Unlike Zelda to Shiek.<br /> <br /> Plus Link's powers ring more Solar to me -- Blazing Solar Bolt and the like.<br /> <br /> Plus Link's theme of being a reborn hero, returning to save the world from strife is closer to Solar than the Lunar themes of being Stewards to a world in crisis.<br /> <br /> Plus the way Lunar Bond works now is much closer for Zelda getting a power-up around Link.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you want to do Link as a Lunar please do! I'd love to see it. It's a cool idea. FMA never posts in their own threads here (they're all reddit cross<br /> -posts), so if this interests you go nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zelda would need to turn into something aside from another Hylian or a human-enough to convince me that she's an example of a Lunar. Specifically, a real-world animal between the size of a field mouse and a tyrannosaur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T16:33:12-08:00","id":1357268,"title":"","content":"Actually for Zelda 64 I'd see Link as Solar, Zelda as Sidereal (steering events mostly out of sight, with Sheik as a Resplendent Destiny), and Ganondorf as Lunar (he is very Attribute based and does turn into a Kaiju HBT form).<br /> <br /> The same mostly holds for Twilight princess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T19:09:02-08:00","id":1357286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357233#post1357233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zelda would need to turn into something aside from another Hylian or a human-enough to convince me that she's an example of a Lunar. Specifically, a real-world animal between the size of a field mouse and a tyrannosaur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it, but I can't agree with it. That's an incredibly specific ability, one that's not found in much source material; to my mind this is like saying that you can't stat someone as a Solar unless they have a totemic anima banner that flairs during times of great exertion and can be seen for miles. Part of adapting a character from one setting to another is fitting them in based as much on feel and seeing how that expresses in a new context.<br /> <br /> ...that said I kind of agree that Lunar is kind of a hard fit for Zelda, thematically, other than the Solar Bond thing with Link. You'd need to reimagine the character with some more agency to really find her a home as an Exalt. Who is she when she's not helping the Hero defeat Ganon? I could imagine a DB version, a Solar version, Lunar version, a Sidereal version, an Exigent version... even just a mortal with a plot device birthright power.<br /> <br /> I could see a Lunar versipn of Link, not because of any incidental animal forms he might have taken on over the years, but because he's sort of a generally-good-at-stuff culture hero that would be good as an Attribute-based Lunar; he's not especially brilliant at any one endeavor, but he's flexible and adaptable and pretty good at anything he needs to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T19:17:44-08:00","id":1357288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357286#post1357286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get it, but I can't agree with it. That's an incredibly specific ability, one that's not found in much source material...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, y'know, <i>just</i> Loki, Odin, Zeus, Dionysus, Proteus, Athena, Sesshoumaru, Beorn, Merlin, the forvalaka, Sun Wukong, the Animorphs, Bear Walkers, Kalku, Runa-uturungu, Boto, and Uirapuru. And many others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-27-2019, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T20:14:58-08:00","id":1357293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357288#post1357288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, y'know, <i>just</i> Loki, Odin, Zeus, Dionysus, Proteus, Athena, Sesshoumaru, Beorn, Merlin, the forvalaka, Sun Wukong, the Animorphs, Bear Walkers, Kalku, Runa-uturungu, Boto, and Uirapuru. And many others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I'm not saying that people-who-turn-into-animals-sometimes don't exist in source material, nor do I have any particular interest in picking apart how Lunar vs. not Lunar each of your examples is. My point, which I don't think is terribly controversial (or confrontational, for that matter), is that the set of characters from other media who make good inspirations for Lunars is larger than the set of characters from other media who have associated animal forms and/or shapeshifting ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T20:58:16-08:00","id":1357302,"title":"","content":"@TheCountAlucard: Though even those would need to be hit with a hammer, some awfully hard, to get them to fit. Prospectives could fit more easily as sorcerers if they don't do it very often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357286#post1357286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get it, but I can't agree with it. That's an incredibly specific ability, one that's not found in much source material; to my mind this is like saying that you can't stat someone as a Solar unless they have a totemic anima banner that flairs during times of great exertion and can be seen for miles. Part of adapting a character from one setting to another is fitting them in based as much on feel and seeing how that expresses in a new context.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Exalted have anima banners. Furthermore, Solars were made with extra-broad inclusion of concepts in mind, making them a poor point of comparison for narrowing down conceptual play experiences. Sidereals were made for a narrower experience, and would be a better point of comparison, like being secret martial art masters or mysterious figures that gather in groups of three to cast auguries (make sure to pack a cauldron to conceal your Lore Charms!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...that said I kind of agree that Lunar is kind of a hard fit for Zelda, thematically, other than the Solar Bond thing with Link. </div> </div> </div>I don't see why the bond was even necessary, frankly. They're not really contrasting opposites; comparisons generally placed Lunars as the space between the two forces of the taiji, not the yin to the Solars' yang. I'm still on 1e with this as an appendicular thing that technically still exists but could have easily been expanded for other Exalted, perhaps dissolved and distributed into Charms like Lovers' Oath (but not just Lovers' Oath).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'd need to reimagine the character with some more agency to really find her a home as an Exalt. Who is she when she's not helping the Hero defeat Ganon? I could imagine a DB version, a Solar version, Lunar version, a Sidereal version, an Exigent version... even just a mortal with a plot device birthright power.<br /> <br /> I could see a Lunar versipn of Link, not because of any incidental animal forms he might have taken on over the years, but because he's sort of a generally-good-at-stuff culture hero that would be good as an Attribute-based Lunar; he's not especially brilliant at any one endeavor, but he's flexible and adaptable and pretty good at anything he needs to do. </div> </div> </div>But for the best-fit character as presented, I think that Epitome has it with making Ganondorf a Lunar. Anything else would probably require an awful lot of effort and probably go way further afield.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T10:54:22-08:00","id":1357376,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of characters who don't turn into animals who you could use as inspiration for a Lunar, but you do have to add &quot;and can turn into an animal now&quot; to them. For example, my friend played a character inspired by Lu Zhishen... Except he can turn into an elephant.<br /> <br /> While many characters can inspire a Lunar, statting them up as a Lunar adds this very significant thing to them. So if this thread is about &quot;how would you represent them&quot; then it doesn't work. What's Zelda's spirit animal?<br /> <br /> You absolutely can play a Lunar inspired by Geralt of Rivia, who turns into a White Wolf, but if the question is &quot;how to stat Geralt&quot; then John is right to do him as a working-enhanced human.<br /> <br /> It's a good point about the anima, of course, but I'd say turning into animals is way more significant than the anima banner. (Although Antman and Spiderman are actually Lunars which you can do with the rules, and can't turn into animals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T13:49:11-08:00","id":1357402,"title":"","content":"Lunars that dont focus on shapeshifting are a thing, and can always use more support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T14:42:09-08:00","id":1357413,"title":"","content":"There's a massive thread on Zelda's spirit animal if you want to google it on a popular forum.<br /> <br /> I was going to go with an argent Loftwing with blue tinged feathers that turns crimson as her anima flared (but Swan, Deer, Horse and Owl are all good associations).<br /> <br /> That said, Zelda as a Sid works better.<br /> <br /> I agree that you could make Geralt a Lunar (or a Solar, or what-have-you -- I'd love to see other people stat him out as an Exalt). But he doesn't feel like an Exalt to me. Same for the Belmonts. And that guy from Far Cry. Drop them into Exalted and I don't think they're going to Exalt -- and if they did Exalt, it'd fundamentally change who the character is.<br /> <br /> Link and Zelda (especial Hyrule Warriors versions) <i>feel</i> Exalted to me. Not like, they could Exalt and nothing would change: they feel like they <i>are </i>Exalted as is. (Maybe Link isn't a Solar, but he's certainly some kind of Exalt which is why I started with Exigent.)<br /> <br /> Very few characters feel that way to me. (I mean, basically everyone from Man With the Iron Fists and/or Kung Fu Panda... but outside of that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T16:19:36-08:00","id":1357423,"title":"","content":"I would put Yrden down as something that forced spirits to materialize, prevented them from dematerializing, and perhaps also slowed foes with some kind of mobility penalty similar to armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T22:26:37-08:00","id":1357458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356915-how-would-you-stat-game-characters?p=1357402#post1357402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars that dont focus on shapeshifting are a thing, and can always use more support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or only shapeshift in other humans. My current Lunar only shapeshift into humans to keep the multiple identitities of her conspiracy. The only animal on her library is her totem (a red panda) and I don\u00b4t plan in getting new animal forms.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T23:54:22-08:00","id":1357473,"title":"","content":"So far my Chiaroscuro Lunars group has <i>one</i> PC with dots in Heart\u2019s Blood, and <i>no</i> PCs with dots in Stolen Faces. The other PCs have four forms between them (not counting their base human appearance): two owls, a desert wolf, and a cobra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}